 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Cursed Circuitry — Innate Technique (6th level)</em></p><p>Starting at 6th level, you can now apply a high performing <em>Circuit</em> to yourself or an object you touch as a bonus action for 2 CE or a willing creature you touch for 5 CE. Your circuit now lasts for 1 hour or 10 minutes if applied to another creature.<br />\n<strong>Improved Efficiency</strong>. The base cost of a feature that requires cursed energy other than <em>Cursed Circuitry</em> features decreases by 3 (min cost of 1). If a feature’s effects depend on how much cursed energy you spend, 1 CE you spend counts as 3 CE (Eg. Spending 2 CE on Cursed Strike counts as 6 CE). This cannot cause the effective cursed energy to be higher than a feature’s output limit.<br />\n<strong>Increased Output</strong>. When a feature allows you to spend additional cursed energy to strengthen the effects, you can spend additional cursed energy up to your proficiency bonus.<br />\n<strong>Enhancement</strong>. If you apply your circuit onto an Object or Cursed Tool, it instead gains two of the following benefits of your choice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The item deals an additional 2d6 necrotic damage on a hit, increasing to 2d10 at 11th level.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The item grants a +3 bonus to AC, increasing to +5 at 11th level.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The cursed energy cost of the tool decreases by 2 (min of 1). This instead decreases cost by 4 at 11th level.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
   "chat": ""
  },
